---
<div class="lab5-workbench" id="lab5-workbench">
  <header class="lab5-head">
    <div><p class="lab5-overline">ECE 385 · EXPERIMENT 05 · SYSTEMVERILOG</p><h3>Inside the SLC-3 datapath.</h3><p>A guided view of the CPU modules, bus controls and memory interface I built for Lab 5.</p></div>
    <div class="lab5-meta"><span>16-BIT CPU</span><span>SPARTAN-7</span><span>FETCH → DECODE → EXECUTE</span></div>
  </header>
  <div class="lab5-toolbar">
    <label class="lab5-select-group" for="lab5-trace"><span>TRACE AN INSTRUCTION</span>
      <select id="lab5-trace" data-trace>
        <option value="fetch">Instruction fetch</option><option value="add">ADD immediate</option><option value="and">AND register</option><option value="not">NOT</option>
        <option value="ldr">LDR (register + offset)</option><option value="str">STR (register + offset)</option>
        <option value="br">BR (conditional)</option><option value="jmp">JMP</option><option value="jsr">JSR</option><option value="pause">PAUSE / Continue</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <div class="lab5-actions">
      <button type="button" data-back aria-label="Previous micro-operation" title="Previous micro-operation">←</button>
      <button type="button" data-next>Next step <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button>
      <button type="button" data-play aria-pressed="false">Play trace</button>
      <button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="lab5-progress"><div class="lab5-progress-title"><span data-trace-title>INSTRUCTION FETCH</span><span data-step-count>STEP 1 / 4</span></div><div class="lab5-progress-steps" data-timeline aria-label="Trace steps"></div></div>
  <div class="lab5-stage">
    <div class="lab5-canvas-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Full SLC-3 datapath diagram. Scroll sideways on smaller screens.">
      <svg class="lab5-svg" viewBox="0 0 1400 1070" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-labelledby="lab5-svg-title">
        <title id="lab5-svg-title">Modified ECE 385 SLC-3 datapath with bus, muxes, address adder, control FSM, registers and I/O subsystem</title>
        <defs>
          <pattern id="lab5-grid" width="26" height="26" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M26 0H0V26" fill="none" stroke="#35463f" stroke-width=".55" opacity=".33"/></pattern>
          <marker id="lab5-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L8 4 L0 8" fill="none" stroke="#758b7d" stroke-width="1.5"/></marker>
        </defs>
        <rect width="1180" height="866" fill="url(#lab5-grid)"/>
        <text class="lab5-region-text" x="60" y="46">CPU.SV / INTERNAL 16-BIT DATAPATH</text>
        <path class="lab5-separator" d="M40 921 H1360" />
        <text class="lab5-region-text" x="60" y="940">PROCESSOR_TOP.SV / MEMORY + PHYSICAL I/O</text>
        {wires.map(w => <path data-wire={w.id} class:list={['lab5-wire',w.heavy && 'lab5-global-bus']} d={w.d}/>)}
        <g class="lab5-bus-label"><rect x="793" y="67" width="176" height="39" rx="4"/><text x="881" y="92" text-anchor="middle">16-BIT CPU BUS</text></g>
        {annotations.map(a=><text class="lab5-annotation" x={a.x} y={a.y}>{a.text}</text>)}
        {nodes.map(n=><g class:list={['lab5-node',n.mux && 'lab5-mux']} data-module={n.id} tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label={'Inspect ' + n.title + ': ' + n.role}>
          {n.mux ? <polygon points={n.x+','+n.y+' '+(n.x+n.w)+','+n.y+' '+(n.x+n.w-13)+','+(n.y+n.h)+' '+(n.x+13)+','+(n.y+n.h)}/> : <rect x={n.x} y={n.y} width={n.w} height={n.h} rx="3"/>}
          <text class="lab5-node-title" x={n.x+(n.mux?24:16)} y={n.y+(n.h>=90?30:22)}>{n.title}</text>
          {n.value && <text class="lab5-node-value" x={n.x+(n.mux?24:16)} y={n.y+(n.h>=90?83:n.h-13)}>{n.value}</text>}
        </g>)}
        <g class="lab5-pins" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="565" cy="87" r="3"/><circle cx="1172" cy="742" r="3"/><circle cx="192" cy="742" r="3"/><circle cx="1350" cy="742" r="3"/></g>
        <text class="lab5-caption" x="1356" y="1058" text-anchor="end">SCHEMATIC ADAPTED FROM LAB 5, FIGURE ON P. 5.8. SIMPLIFIED FOR THE WEB.</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="lab5-diagram-key"><span><i class="lab5-key-on"></i> Active data/control path</span><span><i></i> Unselected connection</span><span>Click a block to inspect it</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="lab5-readouts">
    <section class="lab5-microstep" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
      <div class="lab5-panel-heading"><span>ACTIVE MICRO-OPERATION</span><strong data-current-phase>FETCH / ADDRESS</strong></div>
      <h4 data-current-formula>MAR ← PC</h4>
      <p data-current-explanation>The PC drives the internal bus while the memory address register captures the instruction address.</p>
      <div class="lab5-signals"><span>ASSERTED SIGNALS</span><div data-signal-tags></div></div>
    </section>
    <section class="lab5-module-panel">
      <div class="lab5-panel-heading"><span>MODULE INSPECTOR</span><strong data-module-id>PC</strong></div>
      <h4 data-module-title>Program counter</h4>
      <p data-module-description>Select a datapath component to see what the hardware does and which control signals affect it.</p>
      <div class="lab5-module-source" data-module-source>cpu.sv</div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <div class="lab5-foot">
    <div><strong>What's real here</strong><span>The modules, routing relationships, instruction set and signal names are based on the ECE 385 Lab 5 SLC-3 design.</span></div>
    <div><strong>What's illustrative</strong><span>Instruction traces show representative micro-operations. This is not a live RTL simulation, FPGA connection or clock-accurate BRAM model.</span></div>
  </div>
</div>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/slc3-workbench.css" />
<script is:inline src="/slc3-workbench.js"></script>